<!--
  Author: Kris Hollingsworth
  Class: Math122-Calculus 2
  Date: 5/23/26
  File: E01-C02-02-AnswerValidation.oml
  Description:
    Quick check on notation and definitions for
    Order of a Differential Equation.
  Raw Link: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/DoctorHaitch/doenet-math-problems/main/M122-Calculus-2/E01-C02-02-AnswerValidation.oml
-->
<p>
  Check your work: <answer name="ans">
    <shortDescription>Check your work</shortDescription>
    <award>y=x^2+C</award>
    <award name="missingConstant" credit="0">y=x^2</award>
  </answer>
</p>
<setup>
  <boolean name="check">
    (<matchesPattern pattern="y = x^2 + ()">$ans</matchesPattern> and not($ans.creditAchieved))
  </boolean>
  <boolean name="expression">
    not(<matchesPattern pattern="＿=＿">$ans</matchesPattern>) and ($ans.numSubmissions>0)
  </boolean>
</setup>
<feedback condition="$check">
  Close! But remember to use <m>C</m> for the arbitrary constant!
</feedback>
<feedback condition="$missingConstant">
  Close! But I think you forgot something!
</feedback>
<feedback condition="$expression">
  It seems you've entered an expression. Looking back at the definition of a
  differential equation, it should be a <em>function</em>, which by definition is
  a relationship between indepedent and dependent variables.
</feedback>